# SYNTHETIC fixture. Not a captured sweep.
# Hand-built to be loaded BESIDE fixtures/run-with-samples.nq, which is the
# real 2026-08-22T16:00:00Z sweep of the same endpoint
# (data.kkg.kadaster.nl/query). This run is at 22:00 and records ONLY a
# class sample: no dqv:QualityMeasurement and no sw:NotMeasured fact for the
# endpoint at all.
#
# What the pair reproduces. The two run selections this service makes are
# independent: the newest run that MEASURED an endpoint
# (web/queries/endpoint_measurements.rq) and the newest run that SAMPLED it
# (web/queries/endpoint_content.rq). Loaded together with the 16:00 sweep,
# the verdicts come from 16:00 and the class sample from 22:00, so the page
# and the RDF must attribute each fact to its own sweep. The pair
# run-with-samples.nq + run-declined.nq skews the other way, an older sample
# under a newer sweep that declined the metric.
#
# sw:sampleTruncated is true here for the same reason as in
# fixtures/run-truncated.nq: the size limit that triggers truncation lives
# in the prober and not in this graph, so a two-value truncated sample is
# coherent on its own. Its two values appear in no other fixture, so a test
# can tell which sweep's sample it is looking at.
#
# 12 quads, one run graph (urn:sparqlwatch:run:2026-08-22T22:00:00Z).
